{"answer": "I could not find one definitive current location, so this is partly inferred. The knowledge base shows the footer composed in different places over time. (1) Early design: `prFooter({issueNumber, taskId})` in `agent/src/lib/pr-body.ts` always emits `Lore-Task: <uuid>` and prefixes `Refs #N` when an issue exists (spec 6-dark-factory, T047). (2) Later implementation-loop: the footer is built in the Floor-side pure helpers in `apps/floor/src/work/assembly-run/spec-pr.ts`. `stampLinePr` puts it on the draft, and `readyPrBody` (prose plus footer) recomposes it when the PR is marked ready (PR #1750). (3) Current stations: `apps/stations/src/implementation-loop/open-pr/station.ts` adds the `Closes`/`Lore-Task` footer to the draft. `draft-body.ts` in that folder composes only the body, and the footer stays the caller's. The `mark-ready` station recomposes the body with the footer. The onboard pipeline's `apps/stations/src/onboard/open-pr/` also adds a `Lore-Task` footer. I did not see the code itself, so I can't confirm which of these is the live footer-composing function today.", "sources": ["specs/6-dark-factory/tasks.md (T047)", "specs/external-floor/spec.md (FR11.10, FR12.8, FR12.8a)", "specs/implementation-loop/spec.md (FR14)", "pull-1750", "pull-2731", "pull-2043", "commit-e02ccfca77f3529c2ff5358bff248660eecb8415"]}
```

